Z||000000||Haze_Performance||03-08-2001||01:17 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cnla-img245x221-983761477rollbar.jpg"> <P>Its a Chrome Roll Bar for the 85'. It will match the polished Dash trim & Wheel I have..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Anyone know how A Fiero looks with 84/96 Corvette seats in it? I was thinking about some nice leather Vette seats...I love Mr. Mikes but there becoming alittle common.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P><BR>TFTS  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><I><B>Haze</B></I> <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery (Updated Weekly)</A>||||reg||14
Z||000001||Philphine||03-08-2001||04:45 PM||||a little while back on the vette forum i asked if anyone had put fiero seats in a c3 ('68-'82) vette. one person had but he said he probaly woundn't do it again knowing what it took to do it. newer c4 ('84-'96) vette seats are supposed to fit in c3's ('68-'82) with out too much trouble. i'm thinking if he had trouble putting fiero seats in when c4 seats should be easy, then c4 seats might be hard to get in a fiero.<P>you know...in my head that seemed to make more sence than it dose written down.<BR> ||||reg||1
